sequenceDiagram
    participant Client
    participant S3Gateway as API Gateway (S3Gateway)
    participant FileController
    participant FileService
    participant S3Repository
    participant AWSS3 as AWS S3

    %% Step 1: Client requests pre-signed upload URL
    Client->>S3Gateway: POST /s3/presigned/upload<br/>with file metadata
    S3Gateway->>FileController: Forward request
    FileController->>FileService: Request pre-signed upload URL
    FileService->>S3Repository: Generate pre-signed upload URL
    S3Repository->>AWSS3: Request pre-signed URL from storage provider
    AWSS3-->>S3Repository: Return pre-signed URL
    S3Repository-->>FileService: Return pre-signed URL
    FileService-->>FileController: Return URL
    FileController-->>S3Gateway: Send pre-signed URL
    S3Gateway-->>Client: 200 OK — Pre-signed upload URL returned

    %% Step 2: Client uploads file directly to S3
    Client->>AWSS3: PUT file using pre-signed URL
    AWSS3-->>Client: 200 OK — File uploaded successfully

    %% Step 3: (Optional) Notify backend of upload completion
    Client->>S3Gateway: POST /s3/notifyUploadComplete<br/>with file details
    S3Gateway->>FileController: Forward notification
    FileController->>FileService: Record metadata / publish "file_uploaded" event